From a202f6063805b31d3835b99f674a400a03f19419 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vela <vela@hermes.local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:16:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cognition): gate the pairwise redundancy scan behind
 run_conflict_scan
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

check_redundancy compares every active memory against every other one
(O(n^2) cosine) and persists substitution conflicts, so it belongs to the
conflict scan it feeds. It ran unconditionally: with run_conflict_scan=false
the cycle still paid the full pairwise scan and still wrote its conflicts.

Measured on a 24,074-record store with examples/think_phases.rs:

  decay 0.113 s · consolidation 0.439 s · conflict_escalation 0.000 s
  temporal_drift 0.005 s · redundancy >20 min (the whole cost)
  pattern mining alone 3.4 s (examples/phase1b_perf, cap 1500)

Effect: think() with every phase disabled >14 min -> 0.8 s; with pattern
mining enabled 2.7 s, same pattern_discovered trigger as before.

Regression test (engine/tests/redundancy_gate.rs): a seeded substitution pair
with identical embeddings must leave the conflicts table untouched when the
scan is off, and must produce the conflict when it is on. The second test is
the control that keeps the first from passing vacuously.
